id: pm-0d7ord
title: "Render-ready workspace export and reference dashboard package: bounded graph slices, flow metrics, and milestone ladders consumable by any visualization stack without scraping CLI text"
description: "Far-horizon feature. Agents read pm output directly; humans need pictures. Define a versioned render-ready projection (SDK-first): bounded subgraph slices with typed edges, flow-metric series from pm-pee5, milestone-ladder progress, and fleet attribution from pm-gw6uyq, emitted as documented JSON/NDJSON streams (pm-mav1ak). Ship a reference pm-dashboard package that renders it as a static site; any other stack (Grafana, Observable, custom web UI) consumes the same projection. No daemon: the projection is a read-side materialization on the derived read index (pm-801d). Horizon: far, after the read index and flow metrics land."
type: Feature
status: open
priority: 3
tags[7]: "area:sdk",context-management,dashboard,export,"horizon:far",package,visualization
created_at: "2026-07-26T22:34:43.941Z"
updated_at: "2026-07-27T12:58:20.658Z"
author: "harness:opencode"
estimated_minutes: 900
acceptance_criteria: "A versioned render-ready projection is declared in the SDK with its own schema, so a visualization stack consumes a contract rather than scraping CLI text; The projection covers bounded typed subgraph slices, flow-metric series, milestone-ladder progress and fleet attribution, each with a stated bound so no slice is unbounded at million-item scale; The projection is emitted as documented JSON and NDJSON through the shared row contract, not as a bespoke shape; A reference dashboard package renders the projection as a static site with no daemon and no privileged access, proving the projection is sufficient without CLI access; Projection generation is a read-side materialization over the derived read index and adds no new stored state of its own; A schema-compatibility check fails when the projection changes shape without a version bump"
parent: pm-ugqx
risk: medium
confidence: medium
